<article class="env-lemma" id="05AA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05AA">Lemma <span data-tag="05AA">12.5.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $0 \to M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3 \to 0$ be a complex of $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3 \to 0$ is exact if and only if 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(M_3, N) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(M_2, N) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(M_1, N)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is an exact sequence of abelian groups for all objects $N$ of $\mathcal{A}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$0 \to M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3$ is exact if and only if 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(N, M_1) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(N, M_2) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(N, M_3)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is an exact sequence of abelian groups for all objects $N$ of $\mathcal{A}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: See Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0582" data-tag="0582">10.10.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>